    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:b04d5d61d358e759",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "269e6deda0e1b8056adc0f7f41f875216dab0193ae6996e6f4d752f1d79a8052",
      "text": "After breakfast, continue towards the Northern Pantanal. After lunch in Cuiabá, travel to Poconé, the small town that marks the entrance to the Pantanal. From here, the journey continues along the Transpantaneira Park Road. This is where the journey starts to feel very different. The paved road gives way to dirt, bridges cross the wetlands and the landscape opens up around you. Along the way, there are several stops to look for birds and wildlife and to learn more about the Pantanal. After around 32 km, arrive at Araras Eco Lodge. Following a welcome drink and check-in, take a short walk around the property and learn about the lodge's conservation projects. Then climb the 12-metre Great Egret Lookout for your first view across the surrounding wetlands. After dinner, head outside again for a night walk. Under the Southern Hemisphere sky, the Pantanal takes on a completely different atmosphere, and you never quite know what you might see. (B, L, D)",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "word_exact",
        "fileId": "1kNh04OFL-WUFvScuhfvqmz9QVHCFY2hA",
        "documentSha256": "c35bca73e2de2ebb08f2f58da2537e279732b15834442420a4ff17620ce2ea08",
